---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = 'August 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="PromptDNS terms of service: acceptable use, disclaimers, and subscription terms."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>Acceptance</h2>
      <p>
        By using PromptDNS (the tools, guides, and any subscription services at promptdns.com),
        you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
      </p>
      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        PromptDNS provides free browser-based DNS and domain tools, educational guides, and
        optional paid monitoring subscriptions. Lookups are performed by your browser against
        public DNS-over-HTTPS resolvers.
      </p>
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not use the tools to attack, probe, or enumerate systems you do not own or lack permission to test.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to disrupt, overload, or reverse the service to bypass rate or plan limits.</li>
        <li>Do not misrepresent our results (e.g., forged screenshots of scans) for phishing or fraud.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        DNS data reflects public resolvers at query time and may be cached, delayed, or
        incomplete. Tools and guides are provided "as is," without warranty of accuracy or
        fitness for a particular purpose. Verify critical changes (especially before
        migrations and enforcement policies) against your provider's own records.
      </p>
      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, PromptDNS is not liable for any damages arising
        from use of the tools, guides, or services, including lost mail, downtime, or
        misconfiguration based on our outputs.
      </p>
      <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans are billed monthly or annually in advance, exclude taxes, and can be
        cancelled at any time; access continues until the end of the paid period. Refund
        requests within 14 days of a first payment are honored in full.
      </p>
      <h2>Content ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Our guides, data reports, and code are our intellectual property. You may quote short
        excerpts with attribution and a link; you may not republish full pages or bulk-export
        our content.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; material changes will be noted with a new update date.
        Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Legal questions: <code>legal@promptdns.com</code></p>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify my changes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Run the record lookup to confirm live values, then check the propagation checker for worldwide agreement. Both tools run in your browser.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What TTL should I use?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">3600 seconds is the default. Drop to 300 a day before changes so cutover is quick, then restore.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need an account to use the tools?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: all tools are free forever with no signup. Paid plans add continuous monitoring and alerts.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why do results differ between tools?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Caching: resolvers serve cached answers within TTL. The propagation checker shows which resolvers disagree.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is my data private?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: lookups run in your browser over DNS-over-HTTPS. Nothing is sent to our servers.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I use this for client work?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, commercially. White-label reports are available on the Business plan.</p></details></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
